# Project Structure And Messages Rules

## Project structure first

- Before setting up or changing anything, check the project folder structure and place files in the correct location.
- Do not assume paths; verify existing directories before creating new files or folders.

## Messages directory convention

- Keep success/error text for API, database, server, and model responses in `/messages`.
- Prefer importing message constants from `/messages` files instead of hardcoding user-facing response strings in services, models, or controllers.

## Feature and release tracking

- Follow this version tracking file: `feature-version-template.json`.
- If any new feature or child feature is added, update `feature-version-template.json`.
- After updating any feature, always ask user whether to create a build.

## Release APK naming

- Use this release APK naming format: `app-release-vx.x-date-time.apk`.
- Keep `vx.x` aligned with the release/app version used for that build.
- Keep `date-time` in a sortable format (for example: `YYYYMMDD-HHMM`).

## Example

```js
// Good: centralized message usage
import { API_SUCCESS, API_ERROR } from '../messages/commonMessages';
```
